  "title": "The two/three boundary is a boundary of positivity",
  "subject": "Which three-bit knots are supports of sums over hidden bits of products of two-variable functions, with nonnegative or signed values",
  "conclusion": "With nonnegative values no such sum has a three-bit knot as its support, however many hidden bits it uses; with signed values every one of the 16 classes of three-bit knots is exactly such a sum with one hidden bit, and a clause of any width is one hidden bit (inclusion-exclusion). So the program's rule that two-variable constraints never make a knot holds exactly as long as witnesses cannot cancel.",
